{"id": "EUVD-2026-97701", "enisaUuid": "a8c3f3f5-b06e-3a42-a270-31ae35511e53", "description": "FreeRDP before 3.32.0 contains a double-free vulnerability in nsc_context_initialize_encode() that leaves dangling plane pointers after a partial buffer growth failure. Attackers using a crafted RDP client can negotiate NSCodec with a large desktop geometry to trigger allocation failure, crashing the server during context teardown.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:32:16", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-2hhg-8xx6-v73w", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-before-3.32.0-double-free-via-nscodec-plane-growth-failure"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109257", "GHSA-q56w-xxg8-3cmg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf9b8e11-cacf-3c70-bff2-f25f2215df6f", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7be8035a-cbe1-3c38-9836-37436598be69", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}